-- title:
--   Descent of a K₁(qᵃ)-fixed twisted vector to Γ₁ nebentypus
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$, let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ and let $\Phi$ be a function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb Q})$ of which $g$ is an adelic lift, that is: $\Phi$ is invariant under left multiplication by the global points $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$, invariant under right multiplication by the finite level-one subgroup attached to the ideal $(M)$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, and $\Phi(h)=(g\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$ whenever the finite component of $h$ is trivial and its archimedean component lies in $\mathrm{GL}_2^+(\mathbb R)$. Let $q$ be a prime, let $\eta$ be a character of the ideles of $\mathbb Q$ which is an idele class character, continuous and of finite order, and suppose $\eta$ admits the modulus $(q^b)$ (it is trivial on every idele unit with trivial infinite component whose finite components are units congruent to $1$ modulo the relevant power of each place). Let $a\ge 0$, let $\theta:\mathbb Z_q^\times\to\mathbb C^\times$ be a homomorphism, and let $y$ be a nonzero element of the span attached to the twist $g\mapsto \eta(\det g)\Phi(g)$ which lies in the $\mathbb C$-span of the $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$-translates of the canonical generator, is fixed by the congruence subgroup $K_1(q^a)\subset\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q_q)$, and satisfies $\mathrm{diag}(u,u)\cdot y=\theta(u)y$ for all $u\in\mathbb Z_q^\times$. Put $N=q^{\max(a,1)}\cdot(M/q^{v_q(M)})$. Then there are a Dirichlet character $\varepsilon$ modulo $N$ with values in $\mathbb C$ and a nonzero weight-two cusp form $F$ on $\Gamma_1(N)$ such that $F(\gamma\tau)=\varepsilon(d)(c\tau+d)^2F(\tau)$ for every $\gamma=\begin{pmatrix}*&*\\ c&d\end{pmatrix}\in\Gamma_0(N)$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ and every $\tau$ in the upper half-plane; $\varepsilon(d)=\theta(u)^{-1}$ for every natural number $d$ coprime to $N$ and every $u\in\mathbb Z_q^\times$ whose image in $\mathbb Q_q$ equals $d$; and the function on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})$ underlying $y$ is an adelic lift of $F$ in the corresponding sense for $\Gamma_1(N)$: left $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)$-invariant, right invariant under the finite level-one subgroup of $(N)$, and equal to $(F\mid_2 h_\infty)(i)$ on those $h$ with trivial finite component and positive archimedean determinant.
--
--   This is the descent half of the dictionary between weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_1(N)$ with nebentypus and automorphic functions on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb Q)\backslash\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb A_{\mathbb Q})$ that are right $K_1(N)$-invariant and transform by a character under the local centre, applied to a level vector inside the span generated by a twisted adelic lift. It feeds the passage from local data at $q$ back to classical forms, and is used in the construction of $\Gamma_1$-eigenforms with prescribed nebentypus and Hecke eigenvalues from twists of a given form.
